{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1190557-espionage","id":1190557,"title":"Espionage","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-02-28T20:59:01-08:00","id":1190557,"title":"Espionage","content":"i don't know whether you guys know this or not, but World of Darkness Core and maybe Hunter make one of the best engines for a pure espionage game. 2e Has even enhanced this because defense is useful again and tilts and conditions are DAMN useful. it makes for a combat system that is fast, bloody, and dynamic as hell. I just need to figure a way to port Inspiration points over from Adventure! It models cliffhanger endings pretty well and dramatic editing is almost like the Fate point system in my old beloved Top Secret S.I. You don't even have to steam clean all of the supernatural elements out of the setting. The Americans and the Russians spent millions to find some kind of supernatural edge during the cold war. Who can say definitively that those dollars/rubles were entirely misspent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Actor/Writer/Singer/Plenipotentiary at large. Author of: <a href=\"https://www.blogger.com/blogger.g?blogID=3008077057451163627#allposts/src=sidebar\" target=\"_blank\">Painted Corners</a> <a href=\"https://crankreport.blogspot.com\" target=\"_blank\">The World Famous Crank Report</a>, <a href=\"https://2fistedtales.blogspot.com\" target=\"_blank\">Two-Fisted </a><a href=\"https://2fistedtales.blogspot.com\" target=\"_blank\">tales</a> , <a href=\"https://petesslushpile.blogspot.com\" target=\"_blank\">Pete's Slushpile<br /> </a>Also: I have<a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/11856/Pete-Sears\" target=\"_blank\"> books</a> for sale up at Drive Thru","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83